## FORBIDDEN PATTERNS

Never do the following:

- ❌ Use light/white backgrounds (this skill is dark-only, `color-scheme:dark`)
- ❌ Hardcode a hex color or font-family outside the `:root` token set
- ❌ Show percentages without absolute values
- ❌ Draw a donut without `slicePercent` / a bar without `barValue` (when a value label is expected), or omit the 2px border between donut slices and the background
- ❌ Overcrowd the KPI strip (keep it scannable, typically 4-6 cards)
- ❌ Use `chart.update()` — the lifecycle is dict-of-charts + `destroy()` + recreate
- ❌ Format numbers for the wrong locale
- ❌ Use static widths (always use responsive grids)
- ❌ **Bring this Chart.js/standalone HTML into your production app.** If this
  project has its own canonical charting library/design system for
  production dashboards, that is the target for the final deliverable — this
  skill is PROTOTYPE-ONLY. Keep the two targets separate; never port the
  Chart.js prototype code into the production stack.

### Animation FORBIDDEN

- ❌ **`transform`/`translate`/`translateY`/`scale` on any `:hover`**
  (`.kpi-card`, `.chart-card`, etc.) — hover is ONLY background-color
  esmaecimento, never displacement.
- ❌ **`translateY` (or any transform) on layout entry** — page/tab/section
  never displaces on entry; entry = opacity fade (`opacity:0→1`) or nothing.
  No `fadeInUp`, `.animate-in`/`.delay-N` stagger, or reveal-on-scroll
  transforms.
- ❌ `transition:all` on a card (animates any future `transform`) — scope to
  `transition:background-color .2s, border-color .2s`
- ❌ Add count-up / animated numbers to KPIs (write `textContent` directly)
- ❌ Declare an `animation` block (or touch `Chart.defaults.animation`) for
  bar/doughnut/radar/combo — they must inherit the Chart.js default
- ❌ Let `line` charts use the native draw — they MUST be `animation:false` +
  `applyChartWipe(el, 1300)`
- ❌ Use any easing other than `cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1)` for the line wipe
- ❌ Instantiate a chart inside a hidden `.tab-content{display:none}`
  (zero-size canvas breaks the entry animation) — use lazy-render
- ❌ Add IntersectionObserver / requestAnimationFrame / per-element delay for reveal
- ❌ Invent scatter/bubble entry animations — not covered by this system

